      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What to Do After Wind Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Check from the Ground First: Look around your yard for blown-off asphalt shingles, shingle granules, or downspout debris. Never climb a damaged or wet roof yourself."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Schedule a Free Inspection: Most reputable Utah roofers offer free storm and wind inspections. You can check resources like Wind Damage Repair Guide to see what technicians look for.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "Wind Damage Repair Guide",
                "link": "https://theroofingexperience.com/roof-repair/wind-damage-repair/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document and Review Insurance: Sudden windstorm damage is often covered by homeowners insurance, though policies can feature specific wind/hail deductibles. Ask your contractor for a photo-documented scope of work to submit with your claim.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, tell me:"
